# Choozy Project Rules (Verified Baseline)

## 1) Architecture
- Application type: CSR React SPA.
- Entry flow: `src/index.js` -> `src/app/App.jsx` -> `src/pages/home/ui/HomePage.jsx`.
- Rendering mode: client-only mount via `ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById("root"))` in `src/index.js`.
- Prerender and server-side rendering are not present in the codebase (no `renderToString`, no SSR framework).
- Initial HTML (`public/index.html`) ships with an empty `#root`; visible page content appears only after the JS bundle runs.
- Data flow uses `entities/*/model` and `shared/api/services/apiService.js` with `shared/api/mocks/mockData.js`.

## 2) Folder Structure Responsibilities
- `public`: static template and public assets (`index.html`, `manifest.json`, `robots.txt`). The shell must match the **default** UI locale: `<html lang="hy">` and Armenian title/description (same copy as `homePage.seoTitle` / `homePage.seoDescription` in `shared/i18n/translations.js`) so the no-JS response stays aligned with `LanguageContext` and `PageSeo` after hydration.
- `src/app`: root app composition.
- `src/pages`: page-level composition.
- `src/widgets`: large UI blocks.
- `src/features`: presenter hooks and interaction orchestration.
- `src/entities`: model/data access wrappers.
- `src/shared`: reusable UI, API, assets, i18n.
- `src/contexts`: app-level context providers.
- `src/hooks`: reusable hooks.
- `src/fonts`: local font files.

## 3) Key Patterns To Keep
- MVP-style separation: view (`widgets/pages`) vs presenter (`features`) vs model (`entities`).
- Functional React components with hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`, `useMemo`, `useCallback`, `useRef`).
- Shared async presenter logic via reusable hooks (avoid duplicating the same async state machine).
- Centralized translations through `contexts/LanguageContext` and `shared/i18n`.
- Barrel exports (`index.js`) for module boundaries.

## 4) Stack Constraints
- Runtime: React + ReactDOM + react-scripts + Swiper + react-icons + web-vitals.
- Styling: Tailwind + local CSS modules/files.
- Tests: Testing Library stack.
- Imports use `src` baseUrl aliasing (`jsconfig.json`).

## 5) SEO and Semantic Requirements
### CSR vs SEO (verified)
- Crawlers that execute JavaScript can still index the app after hydration; the first response is still a thin shell (template + static meta only).
- Relying on CSR alone does not populate HTML body before JS; improving `index.html` defaults and in-app document metadata reduces weak snippets when crawlers or previews see the shell first.
- If deep URLs or richer snippets become a priority, plan prerender/SSR or a static export — out of scope until added to the stack.

- Keep a single `<main>` landmark on page composition level.
- Use semantic containers (`<section>`, `<article>`, `<figure>`, `<figcaption>`) for content structure.
- Preserve and extend ARIA where interactive behavior exists.
- Do not mark interactive UI as `aria-hidden="true"`.
- Do not use `role="button"` on actual links.
- Ensure each page has a heading hierarchy with one `<h1>`.
- Keep metadata intentional: page title and description must not remain generic defaults.
- Keep crawlability files updated (`robots.txt`, sitemap references when introduced).

## 6) Routing and Indexing Rules
- SPA routes are defined in `src/app/App.jsx` (`react-router-dom`: `HomePage` at `/`, other paths under `AppLayout` with `Outlet`, `*` → `NotFoundPage`).
- Internal navigation uses `<Link to="...">` (or `navigate`) for registered paths; do not add user-facing path links without a matching `<Route>`.
- For in-page jumps on the home page, stable section anchors (`#id`) remain valid alongside router links.

## 7) Best Practices (Enforced)
- Repeated logic in 3+ places must be extracted into shared hooks/components.
- UI strings should be added through translation keys, not hardcoded in view components.
- Use stable keys in lists (`id`/stable value), never index-based keys when stable keys exist.
- Keep dependency declarations aligned with imports (`package.json` must include used packages).
- Maintain clear separation of concerns across `widgets`, `features`, `entities`, and `shared`.
